# Optional environment for the `python -m ming` development CLI.
# Browser/desktop API settings are configured in the game's Settings menu;
# they do not read these values. Claude, Codex, Grok and Pi use their own local logins.
# Copy to .env and source it, or let ./start.sh source it.
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Pass channel settings explicitly; the CLI does not automatically read these variables:
# --backend api --model <id> --base-url "$OPENAI_BASE_URL" --api-key "$OPENAI_API_KEY"
# --backend pi --model openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol --effort medium
# --month-backend pi --month-model openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol --month-effort high
# Both slots have backend/model/base-url/api-key/effort flags. An incomplete month slot
# uses the whole main channel. No environment model override is used.

# Optional: desktop webview developer tools.
# MING_DEBUG=1
